WEBVTT

00:00:02.560 --> 00:00:06.540
Charlotte and her beloved, the heir to the Arima Foundation.

00:00:06.630 --> 00:00:13.390
I shall take everything from Arima Isshin, and bring my plan that much closer to fruition.

00:00:13.680 --> 00:00:16.480
You've only helped me in that regard,

00:00:16.890 --> 00:00:18.020
Arima Teppei!

00:00:25.270 --> 00:00:25.990
Charl!

00:00:27.270 --> 00:00:28.150
Teppei...

00:00:30.650 --> 00:00:31.370
Teppei!

00:00:35.070 --> 00:00:38.870
<i>Teppei!</i>

00:02:14.810 --> 00:02:18.610
It's kinda lonely.  Is Seika-sama on the rooftop?

00:02:19.200 --> 00:02:22.380
Yes, let's just give her some space.

00:02:23.220 --> 00:02:26.240
Ah, I can't do this anymore! It's a pain.

00:02:26.430 --> 00:02:29.040
What was that, Erika?  How shameful.

00:02:29.040 --> 00:02:30.190
Get a hold of yourself.

00:02:31.610 --> 00:02:35.170
That's right!  Our representative is nervous.

00:02:35.170 --> 00:02:36.970
We must not worry her.

00:02:36.970 --> 00:02:41.140
So long as we, the Social Club administration, give her smooth sailing...

00:02:41.140 --> 00:02:42.770
Huh?

00:02:42.770 --> 00:02:43.720
Who are you?

00:02:43.720 --> 00:02:44.700
Phony Pig.

00:02:44.700 --> 00:02:46.310
I'm Nezu Haruhiko!

00:02:46.770 --> 00:02:49.670
They're currently in the middle of Operation:

00:02:49.670 --> 00:02:52.880
Rescue Charlotte Hazelrink-sama Who Has Been Kidnapped by Traitors of the Earth!

00:02:52.880 --> 00:02:59.110
Think about your first time with Arima-sama, does that make you feel proud of yourself now?

00:02:59.110 --> 00:03:01.790
Didn't we tell you to keep it a secret?

00:03:01.790 --> 00:03:03.630
There are reasons why people do that, piglet.

00:03:03.890 --> 00:03:05.830
I already knew about it.

00:03:05.830 --> 00:03:07.190
Me too!

00:03:10.860 --> 00:03:12.760
Nezu...

00:03:12.760 --> 00:03:17.090
Ladies, let's not be hasty.  It seemed like the right thing to do!

00:03:17.580 --> 00:03:20.550
We think so too.

00:03:20.550 --> 00:03:24.670
It's because Seika-sama has been so uneasy all this time.

00:03:24.670 --> 00:03:26.220
We'll understand if you don't agree with us.

00:03:28.000 --> 00:03:31.030
The only thing representatives worry about is their organization.

00:03:31.600 --> 00:03:34.180
When we have a big ordeal and we're in the midst of an incident,

00:03:34.180 --> 00:03:37.340
isn't that the time we should join together as allies?

00:03:37.340 --> 00:03:40.330
After all, this is the Shiho Academy's Social Club!

00:03:42.500 --> 00:03:44.870
You can be eloquent after all!

00:03:46.440 --> 00:03:49.170
This is the last episode!

00:04:03.280 --> 00:04:06.480
Maybe I should've gone with them after all...

00:04:08.790 --> 00:04:11.130
It's agonizing for women to wait.

00:04:20.990 --> 00:04:22.540
Teppei...

00:04:32.150 --> 00:04:34.890
I didn't hit his body.  Oh well..

00:04:35.360 --> 00:04:37.680
The next step is how I will tell Isshin about this.

00:04:38.480 --> 00:04:39.960
What do you think?

00:04:40.460 --> 00:04:42.200
Charlotte.

00:04:48.560 --> 00:04:51.650
Well, that'll be after you come with me to Hazelrink.

00:04:52.150 --> 00:04:55.710
You can think about it thoroughly when we arrive.

00:04:55.710 --> 00:04:57.900
That must be tight.  I'll cut it for you.

00:05:00.910 --> 00:05:04.420
Well, I'd prefer if you didn't make a scary face.

00:05:04.740 --> 00:05:09.290
Returning Hazelrink's princess and disposing of her kidnapper, the heir of the Arima Group.

00:05:09.720 --> 00:05:13.500
Hartman's single-handed rescue and triumphant return to his home country.

00:05:14.080 --> 00:05:17.130
What are you saying? No one will believe that lie!

00:05:17.830 --> 00:05:22.440
In this world, it doesn't matter if it's a lie or the truth.

00:05:22.440 --> 00:05:25.290
People only believe in those they want to trust.

00:05:25.290 --> 00:05:29.210
If people believe, even lies become truth.

00:05:29.210 --> 00:05:32.850
That is why making people believe is an easy thing to do.

00:05:32.850 --> 00:05:37.310
Yes, that's the truth of this world.

00:05:38.200 --> 00:05:43.320
It's true that people may believe you, but that's because they want to trust you!

00:05:43.960 --> 00:05:48.410
Because people think that people are all wonderful; that there should be no bad people.

00:05:48.410 --> 00:05:50.600
Bearing that in mind, they'd want to trust you!

00:05:50.600 --> 00:05:54.880
As expected of a princess, picking up things one by one.

00:05:54.880 --> 00:05:57.850
Trust and you will not be betrayed, right?

00:05:58.400 --> 00:05:59.460
Yes.

00:06:00.040 --> 00:06:02.430
Thank you for being such a fine lady.

00:06:03.260 --> 00:06:06.940
However, your words will never reach me.

00:06:16.090 --> 00:06:21.780
As First Princess of the Hazelrink Principality, Charlotte Hazelrink, I make a request.

00:06:22.850 --> 00:06:24.790
Allow this person to have medical treatment.

00:06:25.160 --> 00:06:27.810
Unfortunately, I must refuse.

00:06:27.810 --> 00:06:31.430
She loves and believes in you.

00:06:31.430 --> 00:06:32.560
I know.

00:06:32.560 --> 00:06:33.590
Then why not?!

00:06:33.590 --> 00:06:36.690
Why don't <i>you</i> save her, princess?

00:06:36.690 --> 00:06:37.980
I understand.

00:06:44.320 --> 00:06:45.450
Oh?

00:06:45.880 --> 00:06:50.230
Is this your first time carrying a heavy burden on your back?

00:06:50.230 --> 00:06:54.670
Hartman, do you know why I want to save her?

00:06:54.670 --> 00:06:56.120
Not at all.

00:06:56.770 --> 00:07:00.240
If the one I trust the most in this world was here,

00:07:00.820 --> 00:07:03.960
he would surely do the same.

00:07:03.960 --> 00:07:07.320
Arima Teppei would do this.

00:07:14.660 --> 00:07:16.570
Oh? You're finally back?

00:07:16.570 --> 00:07:17.720
My bad, my bad.

00:07:18.630 --> 00:07:20.180
But then, we were waiting for you!

00:07:20.180 --> 00:07:22.350
Goodness, this is an important time, you know!

00:07:22.590 --> 00:07:25.080
You should be by her side.

00:07:33.520 --> 00:07:35.080
Nice catch.

00:07:35.080 --> 00:07:36.670
I thought I was shot.

00:07:36.670 --> 00:07:39.560
Your pansy ass fainted from just a scratch.

00:07:39.560 --> 00:07:40.360
Where's Charl?

00:07:40.660 --> 00:07:43.860
She's in the engine's cab with Hartman.

00:07:43.860 --> 00:07:45.780
Alright, we're going after it.

00:07:45.780 --> 00:07:47.780
Alfred-dono, we're counting on you.

00:07:47.780 --> 00:07:48.730
It's impossible.

00:07:48.730 --> 00:07:49.360
Huh?

00:07:49.770 --> 00:07:53.880
With three people riding, there's no way we can match that speed.

00:07:54.120 --> 00:07:55.410
Brat, get off.

00:07:55.410 --> 00:07:56.590
Are you serious?

00:07:56.590 --> 00:07:57.920
Yes, I am.

00:07:58.290 --> 00:08:02.050
Starting with rock!  Rock, paper, scissors!.

00:08:02.050 --> 00:08:03.160
Alright!

00:08:04.600 --> 00:08:06.200
You bastard, you cheated!

00:08:06.200 --> 00:08:06.820
You didn't wait for me!

00:08:06.820 --> 00:08:09.100
Bogus! Bogus! That one didn't count!

00:08:09.100 --> 00:08:11.200
You said only once!

00:08:11.200 --> 00:08:12.520
The outcome is officially refuted.

00:08:12.520 --> 00:08:14.760
Jeez, I guess we'll do it again.

00:08:14.760 --> 00:08:17.270
Ready, set... Rock, paper...

00:08:17.270 --> 00:08:21.940
Impossible! It shouldn't be possible!

00:08:19.780 --> 00:08:21.050
Sorry!

00:08:26.560 --> 00:08:28.440
What should I do?

00:08:28.440 --> 00:08:29.440
Oh?

00:08:30.870 --> 00:08:32.100
Princess!

00:08:32.100 --> 00:08:33.180
We'll help out.

00:08:33.180 --> 00:08:34.250
You guys-

00:08:34.250 --> 00:08:36.390
We went to a medical school.

00:08:36.390 --> 00:08:37.640
We can provide medical aid.

00:08:40.250 --> 00:08:41.960
Thank you.

00:08:41.960 --> 00:08:45.260
If there is anything I can do, please tell me.

00:08:48.940 --> 00:08:51.440
Yuu-san, it's me. Can you hear me?

00:08:52.550 --> 00:08:53.910
Yuu-san!

00:08:54.320 --> 00:08:56.190
Teppei-sama, are you alright?

00:08:56.540 --> 00:08:58.570
Sorry, I ran into a bit of trouble.

00:08:58.570 --> 00:09:00.440
Give me a route to catch up with them.

00:09:01.140 --> 00:09:03.450
Yes, master.

00:09:03.660 --> 00:09:04.950
Teppei-dono!

00:09:04.950 --> 00:09:06.560
Since we're in a rush, I'll get off.

00:09:06.560 --> 00:09:07.690
No way!

00:09:26.300 --> 00:09:27.540
Teppei-sama.

00:09:27.540 --> 00:09:28.290
Yeah!

00:09:28.790 --> 00:09:29.900
I will guide you.

00:09:29.900 --> 00:09:32.310
After three kilometers, enter the field to your right.

00:09:32.310 --> 00:09:35.080
It's off-road, but you'll be fine on that bike.

00:09:35.080 --> 00:09:35.810
Understood!

00:09:47.880 --> 00:09:51.410
They're taking a shortcut!  Report this to Hartman-sama!

00:09:53.650 --> 00:09:57.540
It has everything, as expected of a government train.

00:09:57.540 --> 00:09:59.870
With this, we can somehow save her life.

00:09:59.870 --> 00:10:01.580
Why did you leave school?

00:10:01.580 --> 00:10:04.300
Ah, we couldn't pay our tuition.

00:10:04.300 --> 00:10:08.910
Our scholarships didn't come through, so we found this job on the net.

00:10:08.910 --> 00:10:11.670
It's an embarrassing story.

00:10:11.670 --> 00:10:13.180
I'm sorry.

00:10:13.180 --> 00:10:15.070
I couldn't do anything.

00:10:15.070 --> 00:10:16.930
You're wrong about that.

00:10:17.250 --> 00:10:20.870
It's true that medical knowledge is necessary.

00:10:20.870 --> 00:10:25.260
But having someone like you to support them, is also important.

00:10:25.260 --> 00:10:26.940
Oh! You said something nice.

00:10:27.230 --> 00:10:28.190
Not really...

00:10:29.040 --> 00:10:30.440
Thank you.

00:10:30.860 --> 00:10:32.700
It's Arima Teppei!

00:10:32.700 --> 00:10:33.740
Teppei!

00:10:34.230 --> 00:10:35.330
What?!

00:11:08.210 --> 00:11:09.150
Here we go!

00:11:12.610 --> 00:11:13.570
Don't shoot!

00:11:13.970 --> 00:11:14.950
It's Charl!

00:11:14.950 --> 00:11:15.740
Alright!

00:11:18.510 --> 00:11:19.580
Charl!

00:11:19.580 --> 00:11:22.380
I knew that you'd be ok!

00:11:26.580 --> 00:11:28.330
Silvie, take the handlebars.

00:11:30.810 --> 00:11:33.410
Wait for me Charl, I'll save you somehow!

00:11:33.410 --> 00:11:33.760
H-hey!

00:11:38.490 --> 00:11:41.100
I'm gonna save Charl and come back. Wait for me.

00:11:41.400 --> 00:11:43.860
Too reckless, as usual.

00:11:43.860 --> 00:11:47.230
But what's that I like about you.

00:11:48.720 --> 00:11:50.100
Silvie!

00:11:50.100 --> 00:11:51.460
Forget the calvary woman.

00:11:51.460 --> 00:11:53.450
Get Arima Teppei!

00:11:56.470 --> 00:12:00.930
You think you'll get far in this narrow train?

00:12:01.410 --> 00:12:03.670
Teppei, Teppei!

00:12:05.640 --> 00:12:06.470
There he is!

00:12:10.830 --> 00:12:12.210
Fire!

00:12:13.260 --> 00:12:15.390
Huh? We're slowing down..

00:12:15.650 --> 00:12:18.580
We're left behind again?!

00:12:18.580 --> 00:12:20.400
What now?

00:12:26.940 --> 00:12:30.720
It'd be a problem if the hostage gets away.

00:12:42.010 --> 00:12:46.170
I'm surprised. I thought you already died.

00:12:46.170 --> 00:12:48.200
My friends saved me.

00:12:48.710 --> 00:12:52.710
In that case, I'll make sure to dispose of you properly.

00:12:53.980 --> 00:12:56.060
So that even your friends won't be able to save you.

00:12:56.060 --> 00:12:57.180
Teppei!

00:12:57.490 --> 00:12:59.630
Don't worry, Charl.

00:12:59.630 --> 00:13:01.790
Have I ever lied to you?

00:13:03.960 --> 00:13:05.410
I'll definitely save you.

00:13:05.410 --> 00:13:06.440
We'll go back together.

00:13:09.620 --> 00:13:10.940
Hartman...

00:13:11.520 --> 00:13:14.450
About what you said earlier... you've been wrong this whole time.

00:13:14.450 --> 00:13:16.200
What are you talking about?

00:13:16.600 --> 00:13:20.450
About the time when you pick pocketed in our hotel and you thought my grandpa got mad at you.

00:13:22.010 --> 00:13:24.860
Grandpa wasn't trying to humiliate you back then.

00:13:25.670 --> 00:13:29.450
What are you talking about? I was genuinely humiliated!

00:13:29.450 --> 00:13:30.420
You're wrong!

00:13:30.420 --> 00:13:31.300
Like hell I am!

00:13:35.470 --> 00:13:38.540
At least I understand what Grandpa was thinking!

00:13:39.030 --> 00:13:40.780
He was waiting for you,

00:13:40.780 --> 00:13:42.410
saying, "Rise to my level!"

00:13:42.410 --> 00:13:44.310
Those are just some pretty words from the rich.

00:13:46.480 --> 00:13:47.750
Teppei!

00:13:47.750 --> 00:13:50.600
The next one is going to hit dead center on your forehead.

00:13:51.000 --> 00:13:55.810
Whether you're poor or rich, it doesn't matter. A person is a person!

00:13:55.810 --> 00:13:57.800
There are both good and bad people.

00:13:57.800 --> 00:13:59.870
I've seen that with my own eyes.

00:14:00.450 --> 00:14:05.150
But grandfather believed that you'd surely rise!

00:14:05.150 --> 00:14:08.620
He believed that if you followed a righteous path, you'd reach his level.

00:14:08.620 --> 00:14:09.880
Silence!

00:14:09.880 --> 00:14:11.120
Didn't I tell you to stop spouting your pretty lies?

00:14:12.500 --> 00:14:13.840
Yuu-san taught me this,

00:14:15.100 --> 00:14:19.010
"The one that decides how far you'll go is you!

00:14:19.770 --> 00:14:23.260
The one that decides what you achieve is you!"

00:14:23.710 --> 00:14:25.900
Seika-san also taught me this,

00:14:26.300 --> 00:14:30.520
"If you work at your social status, an appropriate opportunity will arise!"

00:14:31.020 --> 00:14:33.200
Silvie taught me this,

00:14:33.980 --> 00:14:38.100
"As long as your words are honest, your feelings will be answered!"

00:14:38.100 --> 00:14:44.110
That is why you have to go search for the meaning of your existence!

00:14:44.110 --> 00:14:49.580
You still have another chance to go back and find friends that understand you!

00:14:49.580 --> 00:14:52.740
I told you to stop with your lies!

00:14:58.140 --> 00:14:59.000
What was that?

00:14:59.000 --> 00:14:59.710
An explosion?!

00:15:00.620 --> 00:15:03.790
You will meet your end with me, Arima!

00:15:11.850 --> 00:15:13.550
This is bad.

00:15:13.550 --> 00:15:15.270
Charl, we're gonna run for it.

00:15:15.270 --> 00:15:16.630
What about Hartman?

00:15:16.630 --> 00:15:17.400
That's right.

00:15:17.770 --> 00:15:19.540
You should escape too!

00:15:21.080 --> 00:15:24.400
It's already too late for us all.

00:15:24.400 --> 00:15:28.580
Since it has come to this, I'll tell you something interesting.

00:15:29.260 --> 00:15:33.630
The one who murdered your parents was me!

00:15:35.060 --> 00:15:40.330
Dear me, I didn't realize that Isshin's daughter was still alive.

00:15:40.630 --> 00:15:45.590
What's worse is that killing her son took some time.

00:15:47.890 --> 00:15:48.720
Charl also taught me,

00:15:50.150 --> 00:15:52.260
"If I live on,

00:15:52.260 --> 00:15:55.610
and if I continue thinking of those who are precious to me,

00:15:56.020 --> 00:15:57.710
those people will continue to live on!"

00:15:57.710 --> 00:15:59.720
That's what she taught me!

00:15:59.720 --> 00:16:01.160
Teppei...

00:16:01.490 --> 00:16:04.620
Mom and Dad will continue to live on within me!

00:16:05.190 --> 00:16:08.070
That's why I will forgive everything you've done!

00:16:17.820 --> 00:16:22.870
Rise once more! While you're doing so, think about what's right!

00:16:22.870 --> 00:16:23.710
Teppei...

00:16:23.710 --> 00:16:24.380
Charl...

00:16:25.790 --> 00:16:28.190
Don't be so full of yourself, damn kid.

00:16:28.190 --> 00:16:30.430
It doesn't matter, because everything is ov-

00:16:33.520 --> 00:16:36.360
I told you to restart your life!

00:16:36.360 --> 00:16:37.930
Live on!

00:17:01.970 --> 00:17:03.470
Silvie!

00:17:03.470 --> 00:17:06.090
This where you'd say "nice catch."

00:17:06.090 --> 00:17:08.350
Nice catch!

00:17:09.630 --> 00:17:11.490
Y-You saved me.

00:17:11.490 --> 00:17:14.110
You're not the Princess!

00:17:14.110 --> 00:17:15.720
What are you-

00:17:15.720 --> 00:17:18.300
River shoot!

00:17:43.720 --> 00:17:46.770
S-Sorry about all this, Maria-sama.

00:17:47.530 --> 00:17:48.680
Is it over?

00:17:49.560 --> 00:17:50.750
Yes.

00:17:54.720 --> 00:17:57.140
It's me. The ordeal is over.

00:17:57.560 --> 00:18:02.430
It seems that, Silvie still doesn't know if she wants to stay in this country or not.

00:18:02.430 --> 00:18:07.160
I see, the fight for head of the van Hossen family begins now?

00:18:12.240 --> 00:18:13.470
Teppei!

00:18:13.470 --> 00:18:14.620
Charl!

00:18:18.140 --> 00:18:19.330
Like I said...

00:18:19.330 --> 00:18:23.200
You really came for me!

00:18:23.200 --> 00:18:25.280
Ah, Teppei...

00:18:25.840 --> 00:18:28.210
Charl, what are you doing?

00:18:29.570 --> 00:18:31.540
Showing my appreciation.

00:18:31.540 --> 00:18:33.650
But still, aren't you going too far?

00:18:33.650 --> 00:18:35.970
Because I'm so happy.

00:18:35.970 --> 00:18:38.610
I understand that you're happy.  I'm happy too...

00:18:38.610 --> 00:18:40.220
Then isn't it fine?

00:18:40.220 --> 00:18:42.950
Teppei, come on, come on, come on!

00:18:42.950 --> 00:18:45.270
W-W-Wha?! Charl! That's my-

00:18:45.270 --> 00:18:47.240
Oh, nice to meet you!

00:18:47.730 --> 00:18:50.340
How indecent!

00:18:51.670 --> 00:18:54.570
To all of our concerned Social Club members.

00:18:55.000 --> 00:18:58.360
This morning, they were all confirmed to be safe.

00:18:58.360 --> 00:18:59.950
We have a lot of work to do!

00:19:02.900 --> 00:19:07.090
Thank goodness, Seika-sama is alright.

00:19:15.510 --> 00:19:17.260
Hartman-sama...

00:19:23.690 --> 00:19:24.720
Wow!

00:19:25.190 --> 00:19:27.560
Somehow it feels like it's been a while.

00:19:27.560 --> 00:19:30.870
You're late! The guests have been waiting for you.

00:19:30.870 --> 00:19:34.460
Welcome back, Arima-sama!

00:19:34.460 --> 00:19:37.200
Well, a lot happened on the way back...

00:19:37.200 --> 00:19:39.140
No more excuses.

00:19:39.140 --> 00:19:41.660
Charl, I'm going to borrow him, 'kay?

00:19:42.020 --> 00:19:43.330
Go ahead.

00:19:45.130 --> 00:19:47.370
Huh? What's going on, Seika-san?

00:19:47.370 --> 00:19:51.330
Goodness, do you plan on embarrassing a woman who waited for you?

00:19:51.330 --> 00:19:54.220
Besides, there's a skilled dancer in front of me.

00:19:54.220 --> 00:19:55.930
T-That's not really...

00:20:00.550 --> 00:20:02.890
Thinking about it...

00:20:02.890 --> 00:20:07.090
What if mom and dad were still alive?

00:20:07.090 --> 00:20:10.910
What if I hadn't noticed Charl's carriage?

00:20:11.650 --> 00:20:12.560
What if...

00:20:13.710 --> 00:20:14.420
That's right...

00:20:14.830 --> 00:20:19.680
I could pick from a limitless number of choices, but I am standing here right now.

00:20:19.680 --> 00:20:22.860
That is... a beautiful miracle.

00:20:22.860 --> 00:20:26.750
In the world we live in, there are no "if's".

00:20:26.750 --> 00:20:32.050
This is the place that we chose.

00:20:32.050 --> 00:20:35.070
That's right, this place <i>is</i> a place of miracles.

00:20:35.070 --> 00:20:37.410
We can never change the past.

00:20:37.410 --> 00:20:39.550
Nor can we go back on our decisions.

00:20:39.550 --> 00:20:42.710
This thing called a miracle is our reality.

00:20:42.710 --> 00:20:48.510
We will continue to live on in this reality, forever and ever.

00:20:48.510 --> 00:20:50.670
Right.

00:20:50.670 --> 00:20:53.200
Until the time when you run out of gifts.

00:20:53.200 --> 00:20:55.730
So, let's laugh...

00:20:55.730 --> 00:20:57.620
...from the bottom of our hearts.

00:20:57.620 --> 00:21:04.760
Finally, let's dance upon the stage of this miracle forever.

00:21:04.760 --> 00:21:07.650
Yes, forever!

00:21:16.700 --> 00:21:19.000
We used <i>that</i>  much money this time?

00:21:19.000 --> 00:21:24.570
Yes, we demolished the Grand Hazelrink and wrecked a Fil'mish vineyard.

00:21:24.570 --> 00:21:28.670
Please do not worry about it.
Everything will be taken care of.

00:21:28.870 --> 00:21:32.300
The Arima Financial group will have no problem handling this level of expenses.

00:21:32.300 --> 00:21:33.910
We will pay for everything in full.

00:21:34.210 --> 00:21:37.160
Well, you know, just paying them back with money is kind of...

00:21:37.490 --> 00:21:44.860
In that case, if you address those involved, with an apology and gratitude, wouldn't that suffice?

00:21:53.270 --> 00:21:55.770
As I thought, I'm terrible at planning normal parties.

00:21:57.590 --> 00:21:59.600
Ow-w-w-w.

00:22:03.310 --> 00:22:05.740
Even though it was inevitable...

00:22:06.270 --> 00:22:08.920
I would've shown you more if you came back earlier.

00:22:08.920 --> 00:22:09.320
Huh?

00:22:09.320 --> 00:22:11.120
N-No, it was nothing.

00:22:11.120 --> 00:22:12.410
Oh, that's right.

00:22:13.890 --> 00:22:15.410
An apology?

00:22:15.410 --> 00:22:19.580
Be picky and approach those who were involved. Isn't that your style?

00:22:20.110 --> 00:22:22.230
My style...

00:22:25.250 --> 00:22:27.110
An apology? For me?

00:22:27.110 --> 00:22:28.260
A present?

00:22:28.500 --> 00:22:32.660
I don't need that. If anyone should voice their thanks, then it'd be us.

00:22:32.660 --> 00:22:38.270
Well, since we destroyed a vineyard and caused all kinds of problems for the Fil'mish.

00:22:39.170 --> 00:22:42.420
Maria wants a present from onii-chan!

00:22:42.420 --> 00:22:43.360
Hey Maria!

00:22:44.320 --> 00:22:47.610
Teppei-dono, you should already have someone you can consult this with, right?

00:22:52.960 --> 00:22:54.390
Why are you mad?

00:22:54.390 --> 00:22:56.970
You consulted me last.

00:22:56.970 --> 00:23:01.270
Well, because... I caused the most trouble for your homeland.

00:23:01.270 --> 00:23:04.820
I do not care! There is a difference between first and second!

00:23:04.820 --> 00:23:07.710
You had to concern those menial things...

00:23:07.710 --> 00:23:10.180
To think I was last!

00:23:10.180 --> 00:23:12.040
I'm sorry, ok?

00:23:13.420 --> 00:23:14.850
Just kidding.

00:23:15.130 --> 00:23:17.030
I gave you my answer already.

00:23:17.030 --> 00:23:18.140
Is that right?

00:23:18.520 --> 00:23:22.070
Everything is up to you!
